Add an all-in-one inventory for the deployer.

Running Kolla Ansible from a container on the host it deploys, over
community.docker.nsenter, needs the deploy host not to be named
localhost, so all-in-one cannot simply change its connection. Add
all-in-one-deployer, which names the host kolla.

A host named localhost replaces Ansible's implicit one, and its
ansible_connection overrides the connection: local of tasks delegated
to localhost, sending them to the host. ansible_remote_tmp is absolute
because the plugin passes the container's HOME to the host.

